# Frontend Integration Guide: Notifications Module

 **11. Notifications** and are protected by `get_verified_user` (except broadcast, which requires `get_admin_user`).

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| **GET** | `/api/notifications` | Fetches a paginated list of notifications for the logged-in user, along with the `unread_count`. |
| **GET** | `/api/notifications/unread-count` | Lightweight query specifically for fetching just the badge integer. |
| **PATCH** | `/api/notifications/{id}/read` | Marks a specific notification as read. |
| **POST** | `/api/notifications/mark-all-read` | Marks all of the user's notifications as read. |
| **DELETE**| `/api/notifications/{id}` | Deletes a specific notification from the database. |
| **DELETE**| `/api/notifications/clear-all` | Empties the user's entire notification inbox. |
| **POST** | `/api/notifications/broadcast` | **Admin Only**. Broadcasts a message to target users via multiple channels (In-App, Email, WhatsApp). |

